# GETLOGIN(3)

## NAME

getlogin - get login name

## SYNOPSIS

```c
#include <unistd.h>

char *getlogin(void);
```

## DESCRIPTION

*Getlogin* returns a pointer to the login name as found in */etc/utmp*. It may be used in
conjunction with *getpwnam* to locate the correct password file entry when the same userid is
shared by several login names.

If *getlogin* is called within a process that is not attached to a typewriter, it returns NULL.
The correct procedure for determining the login name is to first call *getlogin* and if it
fails, to call *getpwuid*.

## FILES

| /etc/utmp
| share/besm6/lib/libc.a, lib/libc/gen/getlogin.c

## SEE ALSO

getpwent(3), getgrent(3), utmp(5), ttyname(3)

## DIAGNOSTICS

Returns NULL (0) if name not found.

## BUGS

The return values point to static data whose content is overwritten by each call.

**Note:** this routine stands on ttyslot(3), which stands on ttyname(3), which reads a
directory with an ordinary read(2). So it answers under this kernel and *not* under b6sim,
whose *read* is the host's and refuses a directory. Its failure path is what lib/test covers.

## BESM-6 NOTES

One v7 bug is fixed rather than carried: it wrote **ubuf.ut_name[8] = ' '** - one past the end
of the eight-character field - as a sentinel before scanning back over trailing blanks. The
scan is bounded now instead.
